From a2700061e98d51f4952052a10b8284cc2ff24c70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 14:31:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 513/572] feat(stm32mp1-fdts): Use a generic name for the PMIC
 node

The ePAPR standard says that: "the name of a node should be somewhat
generic, reflecting the function of the device and not its precise
programming model."

So, change the stpmic binding document to use a generic name
with pattern: "^pmic@[0-9]$" and update the associated device tree,
using a alias with the PMICl model: STPMIC1.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 4c5b20bd4f829e50ad299a995df5af0da5361716 feat(stm32mp1-fdts): Use a generic name for the PMIC node]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I3acf995d88385c515067f253b086f760ed76ec28
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/579278
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
